### Finding 1: Wildcard CORS + Credentials on `affiliates.betpanda.io/rest/*`

| Q | Answer |
|---|--------|
| Q1 Scope | **Yes** — "All company-owned infrastructure" in scope.yml |
| Q2 Reachable | **Yes** — public, unauthenticated OPTIONS reflects any origin + ACAC:true |
| Q3 Impact | **Yes** — cross-origin exfiltration of player PII, transactions, commissions; password/payout tampering → ATO |
| Q4 Provable | **Yes** — passive: `OPTIONS -H "Origin: https://evil.com"` confirms ACAO+ACAC; auth-helped: credentialed fetch returns data |
| Q5 Novel | **Yes** — specific wildcard CORS+credentials with 20+ authenticated money-flow endpoints on this gambling affiliate API not previously reported |
| Q6 Not always-rejected | **Yes** — CORS misconfiguration is not on the always-rejected list (descriptive headers/banners are; wildcard CORS with credentials is not) |
| Q7 Reasonable triager | **Yes** — Critical severity, clear exploit path, real-money gambling platform |

**Verdict: VALID**
- **Proof steps:** `curl -sS -D- https://affiliates.betpanda.io/rest/user/players -H "Origin: https://evil.com"` — confirm ACAO reflected + ACAC:true; then authenticated: `curl -b cookies.txt https://affiliates.betpanda.io/rest/user/players -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Origin: https://evil.com" -d '{"limit":1,"offset":0}'` — confirm data returns cross-origin.
- **Impact:** Cross-tenant PII + financial data exfiltration, account takeover via password/payout modification.
- **CVSS 3.1:** 9.1 (Critical) — AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:N
- **Reporting channel:** bugs.olivermaicher.eu

